ness once per minute. It raises `lead_receiver_missing` after an actionable Notice waits 30 seconds without a receiver, then closes that episode when the receiver returns. An unacknowledged User-actionable Notice raises one `notice_delivery_delayed` Notice after one minute, whether delivery is pending or the Lead has not acknowledged it. Acknowledging all overdue Notices closes that alert episode. A missing process is repaired without treating a reboot as an unhealthy heartbeat episode. Stale watches receive SIGTERM and must exit gracefully; supervision never SIGKILLs a watch during Project maintenance. Project maintenance commands, Herdr events, harness hooks and extensions supervise active Project watches. A Pi or OpenCode handoff ensures the independent Project observer is running before its receiver wait, but does not perform observer maintenance inline; adapters own receipt delivery and re-arming. `posse doctor` reports their health, and `posse watch --repair` repairs one without restarting the Lead or Workers. Supervision never starts a watch for a Project marked down. Legacy labelled Watch tabs in the Project workspace are closed during `posse up` and recovery. A 0.14 label is matched only to its recorded pane; unrelated workspaces stay untouched, and an agent occupying a former Watch pane blocks the upgrade. Watch reconcile and watch failures retain the existing visible `pr_watch_failing` behavior; Watch logs and retries transient store contention on the next poll without a Notice. When a held restore, a deferred recovery, an unavailable Herdr or contention keeps the reconcile pass from completing for two minutes, Watch raises one `reconcile_blocked` Notice naming the cause; a completed pass ends the episode. A queued Task's `wait_reason` names that cause while a Worker slot is free. A foreground command that defers reconciliation because its bounded SQLite budget is exhausted continues from durable state and warns that output may be stale. When the recorded Lead pane has been absent for one hour and no Worker is active, the Watch parks the Project: it stops without changing Tasks, Notices or Decisions. `posse` and `posse list --all` show `parked` and the reason; `posse up --all` skips parked Projects and names them, while `posse up` in the Project folder resumes one. A Watch does not deliver Notice alerts to a missing Herdr workspace. [ADR 0025](adr/0025-hidden-supervised-project-watches.md) amends ADR 0001 and narrows ADR 0005's detached-Watch restriction.

 **Watch repair.** From the Project folder, the User can run `posse watch --repair` to restore only its watch, including while its restore is held. It verifies the existing active Lead workspace and one matching process; it updates only watch runtime state and never calls `recoverProject`, changes config, restarts the Lead or starts Workers. Repeating the command is a no-op when the watch is healthy. `posse doctor` reports each active Project's watch PID, executable identity, heartbeat and log path.

